<span id="A6.pic6.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.pic6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Analysis &amp; Critique</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 14.23)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.72em;--ltx-fo-height:12.41em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:9.25pt;" height="161.2" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 158.78)" width="444.39"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A6.pic6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:34.72em;">
<span id="A6.pic6.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.pic6.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Alignment with User Needs (R3):<span id="A6.pic6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
1. </span>Entity Error:<span id="A6.pic6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The Baseline confuses "Baixi" with "West Slope Center".
2. </span>Redundancy:<span id="A6.pic6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It includes excessive irrelevant details (taxi scams, motion sickness) that dilute the answer.
3. </span>Logic Error:<span id="A6.pic6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> It assumes the season is "Summer" without user input. Our model aligns with the user’s specific need for navigation instructions.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8. </span>Case Study 3 showcasing reduction of logical inconsistencies and redundancy in complex tasks</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10473v1/fig3.png" id="A6.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/227;" width="476" height="227" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9. </span>Screenshot of the human annotation interface. The workbench presents the query, user intent analysis, and reference notes. Annotators provide dual-granularity feedback: fine-grained scores on specific dimensions and holistic pairwise rankings.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A6.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5. </span>Detailed Definitions of Multi-Dimensional Reward Criteria.</figcaption>
<div id="A6.T5.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:121.9pt;vertical-align:-59.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-190.9pt,67.4pt) scale(0.474725093095579,0.474725093095579) ;">
